{
  "_comment": [
    "The void crossings: for each region, where you can get to from it and how that fork reads.",
    "Moved out of plugins/voidwalking/index.js so a new connection is a content edit, not an engine one.",
    "key: the destination id, and the SEED of the road (changing one re-rolls that highway).",
    "dest: the zone a walker arrives at. region: the region at the other end. heading/sign: what the fork and the boards say.",
    "dir: which way the walker fork turns for it. Must be unique among the region's destinations.",
    "A region with two entrances offers each destination only from the entrance its road actually uses (gatePair).",
    "Every connection must appear from both ends, and every pair needs a number in routes.json. gl:wildlands checks both.",
    "hub: { toward, distance, ramps } (optional) — every road out of a region runs as ONE trunk `distance` tiles toward `toward` (a compass word, or a bearing in degrees, 0 = north, 90 = east) and branches there. `ramps: false` forks it as a Y (every road carries on from the end of the trunk); otherwise the road that carries straight on continues and the rest leave earlier on slip roads.",
    "gate (optional, on a destination): the zone id of the entrance its road leaves by, to make two roads share one entrance. Otherwise the closest pair of entrances is used."
  ],
